      When planning a custom indoor or outdoor kitchen countertop, the fundamental fork in the road is mix design: should you use inexpensive 60-lb sacks of <strong>Quikrete 5000</strong> from the local home center, or invest in an engineered <strong>Glass Fiber Reinforced Concrete (GFRC)</strong> matrix? Here is the structural engineering breakdown of flexural strength, water-cement ratios, crack resistance, and longevity.
    </p>

