    title="Never Use Standard E-Glass Fiberglass Mesh from Drywall or Marine Boat Repair"
    note="A critical chemistry rule that many ambitious DIY builders miss: Portland cement paste is extraordinarily alkaline, possessing a pH between 12.5 and 13.5 due to dissolved calcium hydroxide. Standard electrical-grade glass fibers (E-glass), such as the rolls of fiberglass drywall tape or marine boat repair fiberglass found at hardware stores, contain high boron and silica content. Under a pH of 13, the alkaline pore solution chemically dissolves standard E-glass within 6 to 18 months, reducing the structural reinforcement to mush. For concrete countertops, you must verify that the fibers are certified Alkali-Resistant (AR) glass with a minimum zirconia (ZrO2) content of 16.5% under ASTM C1666 specifications. Zirconia forms a chemical passivation layer that permanently resists alkaline hydroxide attack."
  />

